Subject: [PATCH 09/44] feat: shutter-linked motion blur, ND filter, bokeh
 forward wiring

- Motion blur now follows the camera shutter (r_MotionBlurShutterSpeed
  = shutter denominator, cvar saved/restored): 1/50 gives the 180 degree
  film look, fast shutters give crisp staccato motion. Closes the gap
  where shutter affected brightness but not blur.
- ND Filter (whole stops): darkens without touching DOF or motion blur
  and starves the sensor slightly for grain, like a real matte box ND.
- Aperture Blades property plus Dof_User_ApertureBlades/Dof_User_FNumber
  post params: inert no-ops on the stock renderer, picked up by the
  upcoming renderer-side polygonal bokeh change. Safe on official DLLs.

Plugin-only freeze point: everything up to here runs on the unmodified
engine. Renderer work starts after this commit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
